│               ├── main.py
│               ├── engine.py
│               └── signals.py
│
└── README.md
```

The structure will evolve as additional modules and capabilities are introduced.

## Technology Stack

| Area | Technology |
|---|---|
| Programming Language | Python |
| Development Environment | PyCharm |
| Version Control | Git / GitHub |
| Configuration | Properties-based configuration |

Additional technologies for market data, analytics, AI integration, persistence and visualisation will be evaluated as the project develops.

## Development Approach

PortfolioPilot is being developed incrementally, following a modular and extensible design approach.

Key engineering priorities include:

- Separation of concerns and modular design
- Reusable analytical components
- Configurable application behaviour
- Testable business and analytical logic
- Extensible integration with external data sources
- Clear separation between analysis, risk evaluation and investment decisions

## Roadmap

Planned development areas:

- [ ] Establish the core application and decision engine
- [ ] Develop market-data integration
- [ ] Expand fundamental and technical analysis
- [ ] Introduce portfolio risk evaluation
- [ ] Develop portfolio allocation and optimisation
- [ ] Add historical backtesting capabilities
- [ ] Explore AI-powered investment research and insights
- [ ] Introduce persistent portfolio data management
- [ ] Develop a user-friendly dashboard
- [ ] Add automated testing and deployment workflows

## Responsible Use

PortfolioPilot is an experimental investment research and decision-support project.

It is not a registered investment adviser, does not guarantee investment returns and is not intended to execute real-money trades without appropriate safeguards and explicit authorisation.

All analytical outputs should be independently evaluated before making investment decisions.

## Project Status

**Early-stage development — actively evolving.**

The repository currently contains the initial application foundation. Further functionality and architectural components will be introduced progressively.

